When a tenant writes from their portal, it
lands in your Inbox — no need to check

2
00:00:08.717 --> 00:00:10.217
each tenant's page.

3
00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:16.220
It shows how long they've been waiting,
and turns urgent after two days without a

4
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:17.720
reply.

5
00:00:17.746 --> 00:00:23.246
The property's managers also get an email
with a link straight to the conversation.

6
00:00:27.918 --> 00:00:31.418
Reply opens the conversation on the
tenant's page.

7
00:00:37.075 --> 00:00:42.365
Answer it here. The tenant sees your reply
in their portal, and the message leaves

8
00:00:42.365 --> 00:00:43.865
your Inbox.

9
00:00:44.241 --> 00:00:49.241
No reply needed? Mark resolved closes it.
If the tenant writes again, it comes back.

10
00:00:51.197 --> 00:00:55.886
Prefer no emails? Switch them off on the
Automations page — the Inbox still shows

11
00:00:55.886 --> 00:00:57.386
every message.

12
00:00:57.386 --> 00:01:00.204
That's tenant messages: in your Inbox,
answered in one place.
